  "description": "VOCLAD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H177 Dy4 Fe7 N6 O40. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 29 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.926-3.977 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.00-134.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C85H171.75Dy4Fe7N6.75O40.75. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 0 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
